; The page records both halves of the fetch path speak: [seekwright.wire],
; wrapped as [Seekwright_wire]. A second small library beside [seekwright.text]
; rather than a module in either big one, for the same reason the walk needed
; one — [seekwright.fetch] produces a fetched page and [seekwright] consumes it,
; and the direction between those two is fixed, so the shared type can sit only
; underneath both.
;
; Stdlib-only like [seekwright.text]: a record of strings, ints, options. It
; names no fetch backend, no grant and no wire model, so the direction
; [mcp-caps → seekwright → seekwright.providers / seekwright.fetch] is unchanged
; with one floor under it.
(library
 (name seekwright_wire)
 (public_name seekwright.wire))
